From: ROCKNIX
Subject: [PATCH] build: drop CONFIG_CONCURRENT_MODE, one wlan interface is enough

Concurrent mode makes the driver register a second, virtual net_device, so the
Miyoo Flip comes up with both wlan0 and wlan1 for a single radio. Nothing in
ROCKNIX wants that. Netplay's access point switches the one interface into AP
mode via iwctl and hands it back afterwards, which is mutually exclusive with
station mode by construction; no script runs AP and station together, and
nothing uses P2P. The other out-of-tree Realtek driver in the tree, RTW88 on
S922X, does not set the flag either.

What the second interface does do is break things.

Userspace picks its device with

  WIFI_DEV="$(ls /sys/class/net | grep -m1 ^wlan)"

in both wifictl and rocknix-info, which is always wlan0. NetworkManager is under
no such constraint and will happily associate on wlan1. When it does, every
wifictl operation is aimed at the wrong device. The one that hurts is `wifictl
pin`, run from sleep.sh before suspend to raise the autoconnect priority of the
network in use: pin_wifi asks wlan0 for its active connection, gets nothing back
and returns without pinning anything. On resume NM then autoconnects to whatever
saved profile it likes, on whichever interface, and the device silently changes
network and DHCP lease. Observed exactly that across suspend cycles -- wlan1 at
one address before, wlan0 at another after, and by the third cycle no link at
all until a reboot.

It is also implicated in the crashes that patches 003 and 004 fix. Both traces
are on wlan1's wdev: 003 notes that suppressing the disconnect on the primary
adapter alone was not enough "because CONFIG_CONCURRENT_MODE gives wlan1 its own
wdev and that is the one in the trace", and 004's reproducer is a plain `nmcli
device disconnect wlan1`. Those patches are still correct and still needed --
the same paths exist for a single interface -- but there is no reason to keep
handing the driver a second wdev to get wrong.

The flag lives in the fork's ccflags-y rather than in a make variable, so it has
to come out here.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -201,5 +201,5 @@
 platform/platform_ops.o \
 core/rtw_mp.o
 
-ccflags-y += -O1 -Wno-unused-variable -Wno-date-time -I$(src)/include -I$(src)/platform -I$(src)/hal/btc -DCONFIG_AP_MODE -DCONFIG_ECSA -DCONFIG_P2P -DCONFIG_MP_INCLUDED -DRTW_IPS_MODE=0 -DRTW_LPS_MODE=0 -DCONFIG_POWER_SAVING -DDBG_CONFIG_ERROR_RESET -DCONFIG_BT_COEXIST -DCONFIG_EFUSE_CONFIG_FILE -DEFUSE_MAP_PATH=\"/system/etc/wifi/wifi_efuse_8733bu.map\" -DWIFIMAC_PATH=\"/data/wifimac.txt\" -DCONFIG_LOAD_PHY_PARA_FROM_FILE -DREALTEK_CONFIG_PATH=\"/lib/firmware/\" -DCONFIG_TXPWR_BY_RATE=1 -DCONFIG_TXPWR_BY_RATE_EN=1 -DCONFIG_TXPWR_LIMIT=1 -DCONFIG_TXPWR_LIMIT_EN=0 -DCONFIG_RTW_EDCCA_MODE_SEL=0 -DCONFIG_RTW_ADAPTIVITY_EN=0 -DCONFIG_RTW_ADAPTIVITY_MODE=0 -DCONFIG_80211D -DCONFIG_RTW_COUNTRY_IE_SLAVE_EN_MODE=0 -DCONFIG_RTW_COUNTRY_IE_SLAVE_FLAGS=0x01 -DCONFIG_IEEE80211W -DCONFIG_WOWLAN -DRTW_WAKEUP_EVENT=0xf -DRTW_SUSPEND_TYPE=0 -DCONFIG_BCN_CNT_CONFIRM_HDL -DRTW_BCN_NEW_MAX_CNT=3 -DCONFIG_LAYER2_ROAMING -DCONFIG_ROAMING_FLAG=0x3 -DCONFIG_ROAM_SCAN_ORDER=52 -DHIGH_ACTIVE_HST2DEV=0 -DCONFIG_WIFI_MONITOR -DCONFIG_RTW_NAPI -DCONFIG_RTW_GRO -DCONFIG_RTW_NETIF_SG -DCONFIG_RTW_DEBUG -DRTW_LOG_LEVEL=4 -DCONFIG_PROC_DEBUG -DCONFIG_RTW_UP_MAPPING_RULE=0 -DDM_ODM_SUPPORT_TYPE=0x04 -DCONFIG_LITTLE_ENDIAN -DCONFIG_IOCTL_CFG80211 -DRTW_USE_CFG80211_STA_EVENT -DCONFIG_CONCURRENT_MODE -DCONFIG_RADIO_WORK -DCONFIG_WAKE_ON_BT -DCONFIG_BCN_CNT_CONFIRM_HDL -I$(src)/hal/phydm -DCONFIG_RTL8733B -DCONFIG_HALMAC_RS -I$(src)/core/crypto
